  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given two permutations (P1,P2,…,PN)(P_1, P_2, \\ldots, P_N)(P1​,P2​,…,PN​) and (Q1,Q2,…,QN)(Q_1, Q_2, \\ldots, Q_N)(Q1​,Q2​,…,QN​) of values from 111 to NNN. Determine if there exists some permutation (R1,R2,…,RN)(R_1, R_2, \\ldots, R_N)(R1​,R2​,…,RN​) of values from 111 to NNN such that the following conditions hold:\n\n\nThe number of inversions of permutation (PR1,PR2,…,PRN)(P_{R_1}, P_{R_2}, \\ldots, P_{R_N})(PR1​​,PR2​​,…,PRN​​) is equal to AAA.\nThe number of inversions of permutation (QR1,QR2,…,QRN)(Q_{R_1}, Q_{R_2}, \\ldots, Q_{R_N})(QR1​​,QR2​​,…,QRN​​) is equal to BBB.\nIf such permutations exist, find any of them.\n\nAs a reminder, the number of inversions of permutation (P1,P2,…,PN)(P_1, P_2, \\ldots, P_N)(P1​,P2​,…,PN​) is defined as the number of integers (i,j)(i, j)(i,j) such that 1≤i&lt;j≤N1 \\le i \\lt j \\le N1≤i&lt;j≤N and Pi&gt;PjP_i \\gt P_jPi​&gt;Pj​.\n\n\nInput Format\n\n\nThe first line contains TTT - the number of test cases. Then the test cases follow.\n\n\n\n\nThe first line of each test case contains three integers NNN, AAA, and BBB.\n\n\n\n\nThe second line of each test case contains NNN integers P1,P2,…,PNP_1, P_2, \\ldots, P_NP1​,P2​,…,PN​ - the permutation PPP.\n\n\n\n\nThe third line of each test case contains NNN integers Q1,Q2,…,QNQ_1, Q_2, \\ldots, Q_NQ1​,Q2​,…,QN​ - the permutation QQQ.\n\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each testcase, if there is no such permutation RRR, output −1-1−1. Otherwise, output NNN integers R1,R2,…,RNR_1, R_2, \\ldots, R_NR1​,R2​,…,RN​.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤10001 \\leq T \\leq 10001≤T≤1000",
      "1≤N≤20001 \\leq N \\leq 20001≤N≤2000",
      "0≤A,B≤N(N−1)20 \\leq A, B \\le \\frac{N(N-1)}{2}0≤A,B≤2N(N−1)​",
      "P1,P2,…,PNP_1, P_2, \\ldots, P_NP1​,P2​,…,PN​ form a permutation of numbers from 111 to NNN",
      "Q1,Q2,…,QNQ_1, Q_2, \\ldots, Q_NQ1​,Q2​,…,QN​ form a permutation of numbers from 111 to NNN",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 600060006000"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
